Imports:
  - Types:
      - Logger
    From: BrowserKit/Sources/Common/Logger

Usages:
  backup_on_write: |
    Before a window's data file is overwritten, the previous copy is saved as a backup file, so
    that a read failure on the primary file can fall back to the last known-good backup instead
    of losing all tab state for that window.
  throttled_writes: |
    Non-forced window-data saves are throttled: a save is scheduled to run once, a fixed delay
    after the throttle window opens, and any additional non-forced save requests that arrive
    while a save is already scheduled are coalesced into that one pending write rather than
    triggering a new disk write each time.

Annotations: |
  This cell owns on-disk persistence of open tabs and windows, so they can be restored after the
  app is killed and relaunched: `WindowData`/`TabData` are the persisted shapes, `TabDataStore`
  persists whole windows (lists of tabs), `TabSessionStore` persists one tab's WebKit session
  restoration blob separately (keyed by tab id, not bundled into `WindowData`), and
  `TabFileManager` is the file-system abstraction both stores are built on.

  Use `backup_on_write` and `throttled_writes` when reasoning about `TabDataStore`'s save path.

---

"TabData(id: UUID, title: String?, siteUrl: String, faviconURL: String?, isPrivate: Bool, lastUsedTime: Date, createdAtTime: Date, temporaryDocumentSession: TemporaryDocumentSession?)":
  location: TabData.swift
  annotations: |
    Persisted snapshot of one tab.

    `id`: stable identifier of the tab
    `title`: page title at the time of saving
    `siteUrl`: URL of the tab's current page
    `faviconURL`: URL of the tab's favicon
    `isPrivate`: whether this is a private-browsing tab
    `lastUsedTime`: when the tab was last the active tab
    `createdAtTime`: when the tab was created
    `temporaryDocumentSession`: map of locally-downloaded temporary document file locations to
    their original source URL, for tabs viewing a downloaded document

"WindowData(id: UUID, activeTabId: UUID, tabData: [TabData])":
  location: WindowData.swift
  annotations: |
    Persisted snapshot of one browser window: which tab is active and the full list of tabs.

    `id`: stable identifier of the window
    `activeTabId`: identifier of the currently selected tab in the window's tab list
    `tabData`: every tab currently open in this window

"TabFileManager()":
  location: TabFileManager.swift
  annotations: |
    File-system operations `TabDataStore`/`TabSessionStore` need, kept behind a protocol so
    persistence logic is testable without touching the real disk.
  methods:
    "tabSessionDataDirectory() -> url:URL?": |
      Directory used to store per-tab session-restoration files.
    "windowDataDirectory(isBackup: Bool) -> url:URL?": |
      Directory used to store window-data files.

      `isBackup`: whether to return the backup directory instead of the primary one
    "contentsOfDirectory(at path: URL) -> urls:[URL]": |
      List the files at `path`.
    "copyItem(at sourceURL: URL, to destinationURL: URL)": |
      Copy a file, overwriting any existing file at the destination.
    "removeAllFilesAt(directory: URL)": |
      Delete every file directly inside `directory`.
    "fileExists(atPath pathURL: URL) -> exists:Bool": |
      Whether a file exists at `pathURL`.
    "createDirectoryAtPath(path: URL)": |
      Create `path`, including any missing intermediate directories.
    "getWindowDataFromPath(path: URL) -> windowData:WindowData?": |
      Decode a `WindowData` value from the JSON file at `path`.
    "writeWindowData(windowData: WindowData, to url: URL)": |
      Encode `windowData` as JSON and write it atomically to `url`.
    "removeFileAt(path: URL)": |
      Delete the file at `path`.

"TabFileManager::DefaultTabFileManager(fileManager: FileManager, logger: Logger)":
  location: TabFileManager.swift
  annotations: |
    Concrete `TabFileManager` backed by the platform's file manager, rooted under the app
    group's shared container so the main app and its extensions see the same tab data.

    `fileManager`: defaults to the platform's default file manager
    `logger`: diagnostic logger; defaults to the app-wide `Logger` singleton

"TabSessionStore()":
  location: TabSessionStore.swift
  annotations: |
    Persists the WebKit session-restoration blob for one tab, separately from `WindowData` so
    large session payloads don't bloat the window-data file.
  methods:
    "saveTabSession(tabID: UUID, sessionData: Data)": |
      Write `sessionData` to the file for `tabID`, creating the containing directory if needed.
    "fetchTabSession(tabID: UUID) -> data:Data?": |
      Read the previously saved session data for `tabID`, if any.
    "deleteUnusedTabSessionData(keeping: [UUID])": |
      Delete every stored session file whose tab id is not in `keeping`.

      `keeping`: ids of tabs that are still open

"TabSessionStore::DefaultTabSessionStore(fileManager: TabFileManager, logger: Logger)":
  location: TabSessionStore.swift
  annotations: |
    Concrete `TabSessionStore`, using `TabFileManager` for disk access.

    `fileManager`: defaults to `DefaultTabFileManager`
    `logger`: diagnostic logger; defaults to the app-wide `Logger` singleton

"TabDataStore()":
  location: TabDataStore.swift
  annotations: |
    Persists and restores whole-window tab lists.
  methods:
    "fetchWindowData(uuid: UUID) -> window:WindowData?": |
      Load the previously saved `WindowData` for `uuid`, falling back to the backup file if the
      primary file is missing or fails to parse.

      Use `backup_on_write` for why a backup file exists to fall back to.
    "saveWindowData(window: WindowData, forced: Bool)": |
      Persist `window`.

      `forced`: when true, write immediately; when false, use the throttled path

      Use `throttled_writes` and `backup_on_write` for the save/backup behavior.
    "clearAllWindowsData()": |
      Delete every saved window-data file, including backups.
    "fetchWindowDataUUIDs() -> uuids:[WindowUUID]": |
      List the UUIDs of every window with saved data on disk, without decoding any of them.
      Cheaper than fetching full `WindowData` when only the id list is needed.
    "removeWindowData(forUUIDs: [WindowUUID])": |
      Delete the saved data for exactly the given window UUIDs, leaving others untouched.

"TabDataStore::DefaultTabDataStore(logger: Logger, fileManager: TabFileManager, throttleTime: UInt64)":
  location: TabDataStore.swift
  annotations: |
    Concrete `TabDataStore`, using `TabFileManager` for disk access and `Logger` for diagnostics
    of save/fetch failures.

    `logger`: diagnostic logger; defaults to the app-wide `Logger` singleton
    `fileManager`: disk-access abstraction; defaults to `DefaultTabFileManager`
    `throttleTime`: delay, in nanoseconds, used by the throttled-save path (see
    `throttled_writes`); defaults to two seconds

